{
  "id": "read-dashboard-panels-read-a-panel",
  "title": "Identify a panel's question",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll connect a panel's title, value, and scale to the question it answers." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "read-memory", "title": "Read the Memory panel", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/3SWXxreWk/grafana-dashboard?viewPanel=22&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "content": "Open the **Memory** gauge on **Grafana Dashboard**." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Find the number and its B suffix. Follow the filled arc around the gauge. Notice that the panel shows one value within a range, not its changes over time." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "The **Memory** panel answers \"How much memory is in use on average over the selected period?\" Its value is a mean and its unit is bytes. Its configured range is a demo setting, not a real server's capacity." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've identified what the panel measures and how it summarizes the selected period. Next, inspect where a panel gets its data." }
  ]
}